<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span lang=3D"EN-US">Hi all <o:p></o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal" style=3D"text-indent:5.25pt"><span lang=3D"EN-US">&n=
bsp;&nbsp;</span><span lang=3D"EN-US" style=3D"font-size:10.0pt;font-family=
:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:black">&nbsp; First, I am s=
o sorry for my mistake for the only one new found hob bug in the report I s=
ent
 out yesterday, it should be Bug 2576 [Hob2] wrong image profile selected a=
fter template load. And now this r</span><span lang=3D"EN-US" style=3D"font=
-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;">eport is=
 more
</span><span lang=3D"EN-US" style=3D"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Aria=
l&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;">complete , cause I integrated the non-x86 r=
e</span><span lang=3D"EN-US" style=3D"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Ar=
ial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:black">port into it.<o:p></o:p></spa=
n></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal" style=3D"text-indent:10.5pt"><span lang=3D"EN-US">Th=
is is the Fullpass test report for Yocto 1.3 20120606 build. There are 16 b=
ugs found in this test circle. We find some meta-intel BSPs failed to build=
 with &quot;Weekly build 1.3_M1 Week 4&quot;, one
 is for connman-gnome and another is for gst-ffmpeg, Due to the issue, QA t=
esting against Sugarbay/eMenlow/Crownbay/FRI2/Huron River is blocked. The 2=
 bugs we reported for these build error are bug 2561 and 2562.<span style=
=3D"color:#1F497D"><o:p></o:p></span></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoPlainText" style=3D"text-indent:10.5pt"><span lang=3D"EN-US"=
>For Hob, a &nbsp;minor issue is that Incorrect image shown when loading te=
mplate file, bug 2576.
<span style=3D"color:#1F497D"><o:p></o:p></span></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoPlainText" style=3D"text-indent:10.5pt"><span lang=3D"EN-US"=
>For Core Build System, there are 10 issues, Mulitilb could not work with l=
sb , sato build and lib32-connman-gnome build; &nbsp;two bugs for Yocto-bsp=
 tools, X can't start in sato image built by
 yocto-bsp tool and fail to build core-image-sato when add patch into the k=
ernel; qemu-native build failed in self-hosted-image with vmdk and gtk-dire=
ctfb image failed.; there is some dispute with the issue lib64-core-image-s=
ato build failed due to sanity check<span style=3D"color:#1F497D">
 ,</span> QA will focus on it whether the case design issue or not.<o:p></o=
:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoPlainText" style=3D"text-indent:10.0pt"><span lang=3D"EN-US"=
 style=3D"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&q=
uot;">For Distribution testing, we tested on three distributions, they are =
Fedora 16,OpenSuse 12.1 and Ubuntu 11.10, and no issue found
 with Yocto build.</span><span lang=3D"EN-US"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoPlainText" style=3D"text-indent:10.5pt"><span lang=3D"EN-US"=
>For ADT, we found three issues that are Segmentation fault on qemuarm ,
</span><span lang=3D"EN-US" style=3D"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Ari=
al&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;">Yocto-bsp tool fail to create Yocto BSP
</span><span lang=3D"EN-US">and ADT-Installer installation issue. Other fea=
tures perform well.<o:p></o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoPlainText" style=3D"text-indent:10.0pt"><span lang=3D"EN-US"=
 style=3D"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&q=
uot;">For Build performance, one qemux86 sato build on a Core i7 machine co=
sts 108 minutes, which is almost the same as the result in 1.2
 M4 RC5 build(111 minutes)</span><span lang=3D"EN-US" style=3D"color:#1F497=
D"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal" style=3D"text-indent:10.5pt"><span lang=3D"EN-US" st=
yle=3D"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot=
;">Note: The test report is archived @
<a href=3D"https://wiki.yoctoproject.org/wiki/Yocto_1.3_Milestone_Test_Repo=
rt">https://wiki.yoctoproject.org/wiki/Yocto_1.3_Milestone_Test_Report</a><=
span style=3D"color:#1F497D"><o:p></o:p></span></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span lang=3D"EN-US" style=3D"color:#1F497D"><o:p>&n=
